sentences.l:
if the kings of the Achaeans, having sprung up, had not seized you,
and Atreus’-son himself, wide-ruling Agamemnon,
took you by the right hand, and spoke a word and called you by name:

So having spoken, he talked round his brother’s wits, the hero,
speaking things fitting, and he obeyed; and then of him
glad attendants from his shoulders took the armour;

And these he himself then wore into the toil of Ares;
but when Lycurgus grew old in his halls,
he gave to Ereuthalion, his dear attendant, to wear;
wearing his armour, that man kept challenging all the best.

But they greatly trembled and were afraid, and no one brought himself to it;
but me my spirit urged on, much-enduring, to fight
in its own boldness; and in birth the youngest was I of all;

for this man will indeed profit the well-greaved Achaeans,
and he himself will profit his own spirit, if he escapes
from hostile war and fearsome fighting.”
